# Roobytes Live Preview

## File map

- `MarkdownBridge.swift` — render / parse / fonts / checkbox draw
- `+CaretMapping.swift` — `markdownCaret`, `attributedLocation`, columns
- `+Folds.swift` — nested-list fold ranges / cues / visibility
- `+Sync.swift` — line-join recovery / decorated-preview detection
- `+Tasks.swift` — task state / markers / undo-jump helpers
- `+Serializer.swift` — attributed → markdown (inline roles)
- `EditorViewController+LivePreview.swift` — restyle + sync invariants + source-line index cache
- `+LivePreviewScroll.swift` — scroll pinning / viewport visibility helpers
- `+LivePreviewGutter.swift` — line-index cache wiring, gutter metrics, bottom overscroll
- `+LivePreviewParagraph.swift` — caret paragraph text/offset helpers
- `+LivePreviewAutoEval.swift` — `=` sum + time-range auto-eval inserts
- `+LivePreviewCelebration.swift` — task-complete confetti anchor

## Active vs decorated

- **Active source line** (Insert / caret line): raw markdown (`+ [ ]`, `#` headings)
- **Inactive lines**: decorated (checkbox attachment, styled headings, etc.)
- Do not reintroduce Source Mode or reverse-convert markdown on Insert typing

### Stale-attribute invariant

`syncLineAtIndex` guards (`looksDecorated`, `isDecoratedBlockLine`, heading-body match) protect against writing decorated glyphs back to markdown. **These guards must NEVER fire on the active source line** (`lineIdx == activeSourceLine`), because that line is always raw text — its `mdBlock` / attributes may be stale from a prior restyle and will mismatch the current raw content.

Violation symptom: user edits in Insert, backspaces past a structural boundary (e.g. deletes `]` from `+ [ ] `), syncs start returning `SKIP decoratedBlock`, all subsequent typing is lost on Escape.

Rule: any new guard added to `syncLineAtIndex` must be wrapped with `lineIdx != activeSourceLine` (or equivalent).

### Newline join / plain duplicates

Deleting the newline after the active raw line joins paragraphs in the view. Sync must **drop the absorbed next markdown line** (`lineIndexAbsorbedAfterJoin`) or the next restyle resurrects it as a plain duplicate (e.g. bullet body + orphaned body text).

Backspace at column 0 joins into the **previous** paragraph. Sync must **merge into that neighbor and delete the active line** (`markdownAfterBackspaceJoin` / `reconcileBackspaceJoin`), then move `activeSourceLine` there — otherwise Esc skips the write (`caret on source line N-1`) and restyles the orphan as a new plain line under the caret.

After any join, **invalidate incremental restyle** and rebuild the attributed string (view line ordinals ≠ markdown indices once a newline was removed). Esc always full-restyles for the same reason.

Never fall back to `currentParagraphText()` for the active line when the caret paragraph’s `mdSourceLine` is a different index (unless reconciling a backspace join into that index).

### Emptied active line

When Insert clears every character on the active line, sync must write `""` into that markdown line (`MarkdownBridge.insertSyncViewLine`). Skipping left stale source that Esc restyles back (deleted glyphs reappear). Only skip when the caret tags a *different* source line.

## Folds

- Nested-list folds hide children in the **view only**; markdown source is unchanged
- View line ordinal ≠ markdown line index under folds
- Sync / restyle / sync-line must resolve paragraphs via **`mdSourceLine`**, never by indexing view lines with a markdown index

## Task marker states

| Marker | State |
|--------|--------|
| `[ ]` | open (undone) |
| `[!]` | focused (undone) |
| `[x]` | done |
| `[~]` | deprecated |

## Caret mapping

- Use `MarkdownBridge` helpers (`markdownCaret`, `attributedLocation`, `contentStartColumn`, `taskState`, fold helpers)
- Do not invent parallel parsers for tasks, URLs, or columns

## Italic round-trip

- PT Mono (and many monospace fonts) lack a true italic. Synthesize the slant with the **`.obliqueness` attribute** (`MarkdownBridge.applyItalicStyle`), never with a transformed font — `NSFont(descriptor:textTransform:)` takes its size from the transform, so an unscaled matrix yields a **1pt font and invisible text**. `.obliqueness` also preserves monospace advances, which caret column mapping depends on.
- Tag italic runs with `mdInline = "italic"` so `+Serializer` keeps `*…*` even when font traits alone would miss them; use `MarkdownBridge.isItalic(attrs)` (trait ∪ skew ∪ role) rather than checking `.italicFontMask` directly
- Underscore italics (`_…_`) render the same as `*…*`; word-interior `_` (`snake_case`) stays literal
